ths old, and partisan-sponsored, so it shifts the estimate only slightly.", "watch": "A stronger-than-expected Democratic wave or lingering Republican divisions from the recount primary could compress the margin.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 67 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Daniel Webster (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Florida's 11th District is an open seat after Republican Daniel Webster's retirement, and it leans Republican by about seven points. Joe Strada won a narrow primary that required a recount, edging Carey Baker by a few hundred votes, and enters the general election with a large financial advantage over Democrat James Pericola. Strada has raised about $5.2 million and holds roughly $2.2 million on hand, while Pericola has raised about $120,000.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the district Solid or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-eight chance. A July poll sponsored by a Democratic firm showed a 42-42 tie, but it predates the primary and is the only public survey. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot. The forecast expects Strada to win by a moderate margin, with uncertainty elevated because polling is thin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1071, "margin": -7.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1312, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1199, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0703, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0839, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0989, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1239, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1092, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0593, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1139, "margin": -8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.126, "mar